ECW2","as_reported":"c.736C > T; p.Arg246*","cdna":"c.736C>T","protein":"p.Arg246*","genomic":"","zygosity":"homozygous","origin":"inherited","consequence":"nonsense","key":"V1"}],"variant_roles":["causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["we identified a homozygous nonsense HECW2 variant: c.736C > T; p.Arg246* in a proband from a Moroccan consanguineous family, with developmental delay, intellectual disability, hypotonia, generalized tonico-clonic seizures and a persistent tilted head.","Thus this study describes the first homozygous HECW2 variant, inherited as an autosomal recessive pattern"],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"},{"id":"R:35753050:1","pmid":"35753050","label":"Caucasian girl","kind":"individual","family":"","n_affected":1,"n_families":1,"sex":"female","ancestry":"Caucasian","consanguinity":"not_stated","onset":"","age_last":"","phenotypes":[{"text":"severe neurodevelopmental disorder","hpo_label":"Neurodevelopmental abnormality","hpo_id":"HP:0012759","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"drug-resistant epilepsy","hpo_label":"Seizure","hpo_id":"HP:0001250","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"hypotonia","hpo_label":"Hypotonia","hpo_id":"HP:0001252","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"severe gastroesophageal reflux","hpo_label":"Gastroesophageal reflux","hpo_id":"HP:0002020","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"brain MRI anomalies","hpo_label":"Abnormal brain morphology","hpo_id":"HP:0012443","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"HECW2","as_reported":"g.197092814_197092824delinsC (r.3766_3917+1del; p.Leu1256_Trp1306del)","cdna":"","protein":"p.Leu1256_Trp1306del","genomic":"g.197092814_197092824delinsC","zygosity":"homozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"splice site; exon 22 skipping, in-frame deletion","key":"V2"}],"variant_roles":["causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["We report the clinical and genetic features of a Caucasian girl who presented a severe neurodevelopmental disorder with drug-resistant epilepsy, hypotonia, severe gastro-esophageal reflux and brain magnetic resonance imaging anomalies.","WES uncovered a novel variant in homozygosis (g.197092814_197092824delinsC) in HECW2 gene that encodes the E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase HECW2.","Thus, this is the first patient with NDHSAL caused by an autosomal recessive splicing variant in HECW2."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"},{"id":"R:40812465:1","pmid":"40812465","label":"6-year-old female proband","kind":"individual","family":"","n_affected":1,"n_families":1,"sex":"female","ancestry":"Afghan","consanguinity":"yes","onset":"","age_last":"6 years","phenotypes":[{"text":"severe microcephaly","hpo_label":"Microcephaly","hpo_id":"HP:0000252","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"hypotonia","hpo_label":"Hypotonia","hpo_id":"HP:0001252","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"failure to thrive","hpo_label":"Failure to thrive","hpo_id":"HP:0001508","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"recurrent seizures","hpo_label":"Seizure","hpo_id":"HP:0001250","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"global neurodevelopmental delay","hpo_label":"Global developmental delay","hpo_id":"HP:0001263","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"cerebral atrophy on MRI","hpo_label":"Cerebral atrophy","hpo_id":"HP:0002059","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"cerebellar atrophy on MRI","hpo_label":"Cerebellar atrophy","hpo_id":"HP:0001272","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"HECW2","as_reported":"c.3601_3602insT, p.Y1201Lfs∗7","cdna":"c.3601_3602insT","protein":"p.Y1201Lfs*7","genomic":"","zygosity":"homozygous","origin":"inherited","consequence":"frameshift","key":"V3"}],"variant_roles":["causal"],"segregation":"Both parents heterozygous carriers and clinically unaffected","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["Here, we report a 6-year-old female proband of consanguineous Afghan descent who presented with severe microcephaly, hypotonia, failure to thrive, recurrent seizures, global neurodevelopmental delay, and brain MRI findings of significant cerebral and cerebellar atrophy.","Whole-exome sequencing revealed a novel homozygous frameshift variant in HECW2 (c.3601_3602insT, p.Y1201Lfs∗7, ClinVar: SCV006279594) in this patient.","In silico analyses and Sanger validation confirmed the pathogenicity of this variant and its autosomal recessive inheritance, with both parents being heterozygous carriers but clinically unaffected."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:40812465:1","pmid":"40812465","section":"pathogenesis","statement":"Dehghanzad et al. (2025) suggested that the homozygous HECW2 frameshift variant likely results in nonsense-mediated mRNA decay. They proposed a loss-of-function mechanism that differs from the mechanism implicated in the missense variants that cause autosomal dominant disease.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["This frameshift variant likely results in nonsense-mediated decay (NMD) of the mRNA, suggesting a loss-of-function mechanism distinct from the mechanism implicated in missense variants that causing the disease with autosomal dominant inheritance."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:35753050:1","pmid":"35753050","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Rodríguez-García et al. (2022) found that the homozygous HECW2 variant disrupted the splice donor site of intron 22, causing skipping of exon 22 (r.3766_3917+1del) and an in-frame deletion (p.Leu1256_Trp1306del). Functional studies showed a twofold increase in RNA expression but a 60% reduction in protein level, suggesting a partial loss-of-function mechanism.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["The homozygous variant of our patient disrupts the splice donor site of intron 22 and causes the elimination of exon 22 (r.3766_3917+1del) leading to an in-frame deletion of the protein (p.Leu1256_Trp1306del).","Functional studies showed a twofold increase of its RNA expression, while the protein expression level was reduced by 60%, suggesting a partial loss-of-function mechanism of pathogenesis."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:35487419:1","pmid":"35487419","section":"inheritance","statement":"Krami et al. (2022) reported the first homozygous HECW2 variant, inherited in an autosomal recessive pattern, in contrast to the previously reported de novo heterozygous HECW2 variants.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["Thus this study describes the first homozygous HECW2 variant, inherited as an autosomal recessive pattern, contrasting with former reported de novo variants found in HECW2 patients."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["HECW2"],"confirmed":["HECW2"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":[]},"candidate_inheritance":["AR"]}